diff --git a/tests/remap/mdi-remap-abort/README b/tests/remap/mdi-remap-abort/README
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..4d3f7c0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/remap/mdi-remap-abort/README
@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@
+Interrupt an MDI command whose remap is mid-execution with an E-stop, a
+machine off, an interpreter re-init (EMC_TASK_PLAN_INIT) and a mode change
+to AUTO and back, instead of an operator abort, then bring the machine back
+and check that milltask is still alive and MDI still works.
+
+Each of these resets the interpreter, which unwinds the remap's call frame.
+Task used to keep its MDI continuation state (mdi_execute_next/_wait/_level)
+and resumed the unwound call once the machine was back in MDI, which
+crashed milltask in Interp::execute_call() for a Python remap.
+
+M400 is an NGC remap that waits on M66; M401 is a Python generator remap
+that keeps yielding INTERP_EXECUTE_FINISH.
